  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on identifying which lottery is more right-skewed (i.e., assigns higher probability to unfavorable outcomes) and prefers the more right-skewed one. Lottery B is more right-skewed (55% chance of 0), and the reason would select B. However, the individual expresses aversion to the low (sub-50%) chance of winning in B and is drawn to the high (90%) chance in A. This suggests they are reacting negatively to the right-skewness of B, not favoring it. The information considered by the individual (probability of winning, emotional reaction to probabilities) overlaps partially with the data needed for skewness (probabilities and outcomes), but their evaluation is opposite in direction: they prefer high-probability wins (left-skewed), while the reason prefers more right-skewed lotteries. Their justification is inconsistent with the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, it is certain that the individual did not use this decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
